course: dictionary
lesson: 2897
title: Doubtfully: showing you are not sure
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words ending in -ly tell you how something is done. Doubt means not being sure, so doubtfully means in a way that shows you are not sure.
explain: «"Are you sure?" she asked doubtfully.» The word asked tells you someone is speaking, and doubtfully tells you how. Try swapping in «not sure» and the sentence still works, so your meaning is right.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Alice often speaks doubtfully in Wonderland, because so many strange things are said to her. Words like say, look, ask and shake your head often come with it. A character who shakes their head doubtfully is not quite sure.
explain: Stories often use this word to show doubt without the character saying «I don't believe you». The reader works it out from how the character speaks or looks.
fact: Doubtfully means in a way that shows you are not sure, or do not quite believe something.
fact: It can also mean in a way that is uncertain or unlikely.
fact: Doubt means not being sure, so doubtfully is built from doubt.
fact: Alice says «I—I'm a little girl», rather doubtfully, because she has changed so many times that day.
fact: «Dubiously» means the same as doubtfully, as in the Rat's «Very good news indeed, if only—if only——».
exercise: «"Are you sure?" she asked doubtfully.» What does doubtfully show about Alice? | *She is not sure | She is falling asleep | She is very happy | She is shouting angrily
exercise: Alice says she is a little girl, rather doubtfully. Why might she say it doubtfully? | Because the Rat told her a joke | Because she is certain of who she is | *Because so many strange things have changed her that day | Because she has just won a prize
exercise: The Rat says, «Very good news indeed, if only—if only——», dubiously. What does dubiously mean here? | *In a way that shows he is not sure | Very quickly and happily | Loudly and proudly | Without saying a word
test: A character who shakes their head doubtfully is probably | Agreeing completely | Shouting for joy | Fast asleep | *Not quite sure
test: Which sentence uses doubtfully correctly? | She laughed doubtfully at the funny joke | *"Is that really true?" he asked doubtfully | The cake was baked doubtfully | The sun rose doubtfully over the hills
exam: Which word means the same as doubtfully when you are not sure? | Certainly | *Dubiously | Loudly | Happily
